2.4 Grouped Query Attention (GQA)
Grouped Query Attention (GQA) (Ainslie et al., 2023) generalizes MHA and MQA by grouping heads. Specifically, we partition the h total heads into G groups. Each group has a single set of keys and values, but each individual head within that group still retains its own query projection. Formally, if g(i) maps a head i ∈ [h] to its group index g ∈ [G], then:
